      "description": "Pill segmented control in figures; pressed state takes the Swell fill.",
      "html": "<div style=\"display:flex;gap:8px\"><button class=\"ds-chip\" aria-pressed=\"true\">By volume</button><button class=\"ds-chip\" aria-pressed=\"false\">By share</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-chip{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;min-height:32px;padding:4px 14px;border:1px solid var(--rule-strong,#2a4157);border-radius:999px;background:transparent;color:var(--ink-2,#a8bccc);font:500 0.875rem Archivo,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;cursor:pointer;white-space:nowrap;transition:transform 100ms cubic-bezier(.23,1,.32,1),background-color 160ms ease,color 160ms ease,border-color 160ms ease}.ds-chip[aria-pressed=\"true\"]{background:var(--swell,#12243a);border-color:color-mix(in oklab,var(--moon,#d6e4ff) 45%,transparent);color:var(--ink,#e7eff6)}.ds-chip:not([aria-pressed=\"true\"]):hover{color:var(--ink,#e7eff6);border-color:var(--ink-3,#7d95a8)}.ds-chip:active{transform:scale(.97)}.ds-chip:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--moon,#d6e4ff);outline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Bridge Next",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "bridge-next",
      "description": "The pill that closes a chapter and leads to the next one.",
      "html": "<a class=\"ds-bridge-next\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-bridge-num\">2</span><span>Currents</span><svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M2 8h11M9 4l4 4-4 4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg></a>",
      "css": ".ds-bridge-next{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;height:44px;padding:0 14px 0 18px;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid var(--rule-strong,#2a4157);background:var(--cloth,#0c1926);color:var(--ink,#e7eff6);text-decoration:none;font:500 0.875rem Archivo,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;transition:transform 100ms cubic-bezier(.23,1,.32,1),border-color 160ms ease,background-color 160ms ease}.ds-bridge-num{font-family:\"JetBrains Mono\",ui-monospace,monospace;color:var(--ink-3,#7d95a8)}.ds-bridge-next svg{color:var(--ink-2,#a8bccc);transition:transform 160ms cubic-bezier(.23,1,.32,1)}.ds-bridge-next:hover{border-color:var(--ink-3,#7d95a8);background:var(--swell,#12243a)}.ds-bridge-next:hover svg{transform:translateX(2px)}.ds-bridge-next:active{transform:scale(.97)}.ds-bridge-next:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--moon,#d6e4ff);outline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Claim",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "claim",
      "description": "Inline prose button that lights its evidence: teal underline that fills on use.",
      "html": "<p class=\"ds-prose\">Two hubs <button class=\"ds-claim\" aria-pressed=\"false\">own the weak layer</button> and one <button class=\"ds-claim\" aria-pressed=\"true\">bridges both</button>.</p>",
      "css": ".ds-prose{color:var(--ink-2,#a8bccc);font:400 1rem/1.65 Archivo,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;background:var(--ground,#07111b);padding:16px}.ds-claim{font:inherit;color:var(--ink,#e7eff6);font-weight:500;border:0;padding:0 1px;cursor:pointer;border-radius:2px;background:linear-gradient(color-mix(in oklab,#17a99c 30%,transparent),color-mix(in oklab,#17a99c 30%,transparent)) 0 100%/100% 0 no-repeat,linear-gradient(#17a99c,#17a99c) 0 100%/100% 1.5px no-repeat;transition:background-size 240ms cubic-bezier(.23,1,.32,1)}.ds-claim:hover,.ds-claim[aria-pressed=\"true\"]{background-size:100% 100%,100% 1.5px}.ds-claim:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--moon,#d6e4ff);outline-offset:3px;border-radius:4px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Site Navigation",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "nav-link",
      "description": "Sticky translucent header; pill links with a flag and mono MC count; active takes the Swell fill.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-nav\"><a class=\"ds-nav-link ds-active\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-mc\">MC1</span> The weak layer</a><a class=\"ds-nav-link\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-mc\">MC2</span> Currents</a><a class=\"ds-nav-link\" href=\"#\">Method</a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-nav{display:flex;gap:4px;padding:12px 16px;background:color-mix(in oklab,#07111b 78%,transparent);backdrop-filter:blur(14px);border-bottom:1px solid color-mix(in oklab,#1a2d40 70%,transparent)}.ds-nav-link{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:8px 12px;min-height:40px;text-decoration:none;font:500 0.875rem Archivo,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--ink-2,#a8bccc);border-radius:999px;transition:background-color 160ms ease,color 160ms ease}.ds-mc{font-family:\"JetBrains Mono\",ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.75rem;color:var(--ink-3,#7d95a8)}.ds-nav-link.ds-active{background:var(--swell,#12243a);color:var(--ink,#e7eff6)}.ds-nav-link.ds-active .ds-mc{color:var(--moon,#d6e4ff)}.ds-nav-link:not(.ds-active):hover{color:var(--ink,#e7eff6)}.ds-nav-link:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--moon,#d6e4ff);outline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Scroll Step",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "step",
      "description": "A story step on the dark: hairline left rule, inactive at 0.4, active in moonlight.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-steps\"><div class=\"ds-step\"><h3 class=\"ds-step-t\">The sky of owners</h3><p>Every light is a company or person.</p></div><div class=\"ds-step ds-on\"><h3 class=\"ds-step-t\">A weak layer</h3><p>Most edges are thin; a few hubs carry the weight.</p></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-steps{display:grid;gap:32px;background:var(--ground,#07111b);padding:24px}.ds-step{padding:8px 0 8px 24px;border-left:1px solid var(--rule-strong,#2a4157);opacity:.4;color:var(--ink-2,#a8bccc);font:400 1rem/1.6 Archivo,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;transition:opacity 240ms cubic-bezier(.23,1,.32,1),border-color 240ms cubic-bezier(.23,1,.32,1)}.ds-step:hover{opacity:.7}.ds-step.ds-on{opacity:1;border-left-color:var(--moon,#d6e4ff)}.ds-step-t{margin:0 0 12px;font:500 1.5rem/1.15 \"Bodoni Moda\",Didot,Georgia,serif;font-optical-sizing:auto;color:var(--ink,#e7eff6)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tooltip",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "tooltip",
      "description": "Floating pane over the water: blurred Raised Water, Float shadow, mono values.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-tip\"><strong>Mar de la Vida OJSC</strong><div class=\"ds-row\"><span>Degree</span><span>48</span></div><div class=\"ds-row\"><span>Percentile</span><span>99.8</span></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-tip{max-width:300px;padding:12px 16px;background:color-mix(in oklab,#0c1926 92%,transparent);backdrop-filter:blur(14px);color:var(--ink,#e7eff6);font:400 .875rem/1.45 Archivo,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;border-radius:8px;box-shadow:0 12px 32px -12px rgb(0 0 0/.7),0 0 0 1px rgb(214 228 255/.08)}.ds-tip strong{display:block;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:2px}.ds-row{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;color:var(--ink-2,#a8bccc)}.ds-row>:last-child{font-family:\"JetBrains Mono\",ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.8125rem;color:var(--ink,#e7eff6)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Stage Corners",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Lit key (colour plus label or ring) bottom-left and a mono count bottom-right inside every stage.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-stage\"><ul class=\"ds-key\"><li><svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"-7 -7 14 14\"><circle r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#17a99c\"/></svg>Company</li><li><svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"-7 -7 14 14\"><circle r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#e04870\"/><circle r=\"5.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e04870\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/></svg>Suspect</li></ul><p class=\"ds-count\"><b>3,428</b> entities</p></div>",
      "css": ".ds-stage{position:relative;height:120px;background:var(--abyss,#050c14);display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-end;padding:12px}.ds-key{display:flex;gap:4px 16px;margin:0;padding:0;list-style:none;font:400 .75rem Archivo,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--ink-2,#a8bccc);text-shadow:0 1px 3px rgb(5 12 20/.95)}.ds-key li{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px}.ds-count{margin:0;font:400 .75rem \"JetBrains Mono\",ui-monospace,monospace;color:var(--ink-3,#7d95a8);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-count b{font-weight:400;color:var(--ink,#e7eff6)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Compact Verdict Hoist",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Opener hoist: single column of buttons on a hairline halyard, flag, name, verdict and confidence on one line.",
      "html": "<ol class=\"ds-hoist\"><li><button class=\"ds-hrow\"><svg class=\"ds-flag\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 60 45\"><rect width=\"30\" height=\"22.5\" fill=\"#ffc61a\"/><rect x=\"30\" width=\"30\" height=\"22.5\" fill=\"#0a0f16\"/><rect y=\"22.5\" width=\"30\" height=\"22.5\" fill=\"#0a0f16\"/><rect x=\"30\" y=\"22.5\" width=\"30\" height=\"22.5\" fill=\"#ffc61a\"/><rect width=\"60\" height=\"45\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c7d4e4\" stroke-width=\"1\" vector-effect=\"non-scaling-stroke\"/></svg><span class=\"ds-hname\">Mar de la Vida OJSC</span><span class=\"ds-hverdict\">Suspect · high confidence</span></button></li></ol>",
      "css": ".ds-hoist{position:relative;list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;max-width:30rem;background:var(--ground,#07111b)}.ds-hoist::before{content:\"\";position:absolute;left:0;top:6px;bottom:6px;width:1px;background:var(--rule-strong,#2a4157)}.ds-hrow{all:unset;box-sizing:border-box;position:relative;display:grid;grid-template-columns:24px minmax(0,1fr);column-gap:12px;align-items:center;width:100%;min-height:44px;padding:6px 0 6px 16px;cursor:pointer;transition:transform 100ms cubic-bezier(.23,1,.32,1)}.ds-hrow::before{content:\"\";position:absolute;left:0;top:50%;width:16px;border-top:1px solid var(--rule-strong,#2a4157)}.ds-flag{grid-row:span 2;transform-origin:left center;transition:transform 240ms cubic-bezier(.23,1,.32,1)}.ds-hname{font:500 1rem/1.3 Archivo,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--ink,#e7eff6);white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:transparent;text-underline-offset:.2em;transition:text-decoration-color 160ms ease}.ds-hverdict{font:400 .8125rem/1.35 Archivo,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--ink-2,#a8bccc)}.ds-hrow:hover .ds-hname{text-decoration-color:currentColor}.ds-hrow:hover .ds-flag{transform:skewY(-3deg) scaleX(1.04)}.ds-hrow:active{transform:scale(.985)}.ds-hrow:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--moon,#d6e4ff);outline-offset:2px;border-radius:4px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Night Sea",
    "overview": "Illegal fishing happens after dark, and the evidence is read the same way. The page is abyssal water. Every finding is a light on it: thousands of entities drawn as additive glow on canvas stages, verdicts hoisted as International Code of Signals flags that act as lamps. The visualization is the page, so there are no boxed reports and no dashboard panels. Each challenge is a chapter told on a full-height sticky stage, text steps scroll past and drive it, and every claim in the prose lights its own evidence.\n\nThe system holds to the craft of the user's VAST22 site but has its own identity. Story typography is a high-contrast Didone, Bodoni Moda, set like chart lettering. The interface runs in Archivo and measurements in JetBrains Mono. The chrome (header, rail, controls, figure furniture) stays quiet: hairlines, moonlight text, no glow. Light is reserved for data that stands for light and for the signal lamps. Density is low on the page and high on the stage. The prose column stays narrow and calm, and the stage beside it is crowded with marks.\n\nThe world refuses two things: the boxed report (cards, framed figures, panel grids) and the neon dashboard (glowing chrome, gradients on controls, saturated UI color).",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Dark, single-scheme world (`color-scheme: dark`). There is no light mode.",
      "Light lives only in data (additive canvas glow) and in signal lamps (verdict flags); chrome never glows.",
      "Four validated categorical lamp hues, each with a lit core variant for canvas.",
      "Bodoni Moda tells the story, Archivo runs the interface, JetBrains Mono carries numbers.",
      "Chapters are scroll stories: an opener with a full-height stage, sticky steps, Q acts with frameless figures, and a closing bridge.",
      "Motion is slow for story (1200 ms), fast for UI (160 to 240 ms), and snaps under reduced motion."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Chrome Never Glows Rule",
        "body": "Glow (additive blending, colored drop-shadows, lit cores) belongs to data that stands for light and to the verdict lamps. Headers, rails, buttons, chips and figure furniture get hairlines and moonlight text only. The dark `halo` text-shadow is a legibility scrim over stages, not a glow.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Second Encoding Rule",
        "body": "The four lamp hues passed the dataviz validator on #07111b for all pairs, but teal and rose fall in the colour-vision-deficiency warning band. Every categorical mark therefore carries a second channel: shape for entity types (square, circle, diamond, triangle, hex, cross), a label in stage keys, or a dash for lines. Verdict lamps always come with a flag and a written verdict.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Moonlight Is Not a Series Rule",
        "body": "Moonlight is the neutral. When series-5 is used at all, it is outlined (fills) or dashed (`4 3`, lines) and never stands for a category on its own color.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Fixed Order Rule",
        "body": "Categorical slots are assigned in validated order and follow the entity, not its rank. They are never cycled.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sturdy Small Serif Rule",
        "body": "Bodoni Moda's hairlines break up on the dark below about 28px. Serif settings at title size and below (h3, h4, step titles, the subtitle, stage labels, the wordmark) use weight 500 with optical sizing on. Display sizes stay at 400.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Serif Tells, Sans Operates Rule",
        "body": "Bodoni Moda is for story voice only: titles, takeaways, step titles, and italic names in the stage. Anything under about 20px that is read for information, and anything you operate (figure titles, compact hoist names, nav, buttons, chips, axis text, data labels), is Archivo. The only small serif is the 17px italic stage label and the chapter subtitle, both at weight 500.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Is for Measurements Rule",
        "body": "JetBrains Mono sets numbers, ids and codes, and never prose.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Archivo Minus Rule",
        "body": "A minus sign in serif text is set in Archivo, because Bodoni Moda's minus is a hairline.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Light Is Data Rule",
        "body": "If something glows, it is either a datum that represents light or a verdict lamp. The test: remove the glow, and if the meaning is unchanged the glow was decoration and has to go.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do set every page on Night Water (#07111b) with Moonlight text, and keep raised surfaces to Raised Water and Swell.",
      "Do put light only into data and verdict lamps: canvas marks drawn with `lighter` compositing and lit cores, and flags with lamp glow.",
      "Do pair every categorical color with a second encoding (shape, label or dash). Teal and rose must never be told apart by color alone.",
      "Do assign categorical slots in fixed order (teal, amber, rose, blue) so the color follows the entity.",
      "Do use Bodoni Moda at weight 500 with optical sizing for any serif under about 28px, and Archivo for anything operated or under about 20px.",
      "Do build each chapter as opener, then sticky scroll story, then Q acts, then bridge, with the story-progress line and n / p keys.",
      "Do name structures inside the stage with 17px Bodoni italic labels, and keep keys and mono counts in the stage corners.",
      "Do pin the stage under `--header-h` above the steps on phones.",
      "Do pause canvases off screen and snap all story motion under reduced motion."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't make chrome glow. Use no colored shadows, gradients or lit cores on the header, rail, chips, buttons or figure furniture.",
      "Don't frame figures in cards, borders or panels. The data sits on the water.",
      "Don't use moonlight as a series color or treat it as a category.",
      "Don't use lit variants (lit-1 to lit-4) as flat DOM fills. They are cores for additive canvas glow.",
      "Don't set Bodoni Moda at weight 400 below about 28px. Its hairlines break up on the dark.",
      "Don't use JetBrains Mono for prose.",
      "Don't let scroll steps cover the stage, or put the steps in cards.",
      "Don't introduce a light theme. The world is single-scheme dark."
    ]
  }
}